1️⃣ Selection Sort (Greedy Approach)
Selection sort is considered greedy because it selects the minimum element at each step and places it in the correct position.

⚙️ How it Works
Start from first element.
Find the smallest element in the remaining array.
Swap it with current position.
Move to next position and repeat.
💡 Key Point
Always picks locally smallest element → greedy choice.
Time Complexity: O(n²)

2️⃣ Minimum Spanning Tree (MST)
An MST is a subset of edges in a graph that:
Connects all vertices
Has minimum total weight
Contains no cycles

⚙️ How it Works
Start with empty tree
Add edges with minimum weight
Avoid cycles
Continue until all vertices are connected


💡 Key Point
Greedy because we always pick the smallest edge

3️⃣ Single Source Shortest Path (SSSP)
Find the shortest path from one source node to all other nodes in a graph.

⚙️ How it Works (General)
Start from source node
Assign distance = 0 to source, ∞ to others
Update distances by choosing minimum cost paths
Repeat until all nodes are covered

💡 Key Point
Greedy when using Dijkstra’s algorithm

4️⃣ Job Scheduling Problem
Given jobs with:
Deadlines
Profits

Goal: Maximize total profit by scheduling jobs.

⚙️ How it Works
Sort jobs by profit (descending)
Pick highest profit job first
Assign it to latest possible free slot before deadline
Repeat for remaining jobs

💡 Key Point
Always picks highest profit job first

5️⃣ Prim’s Algorithm (MST)
Builds MST by growing a tree from a starting node.

⚙️ How it Works
Start from any node
Select the minimum weight edge connecting tree to new vertex
Add that vertex to tree
Repeat until all vertices are included

💡 Key Point
Works like expanding tree step-by-step
Uses priority queue

6️⃣ Kruskal’s Algorithm (MST)
Builds MST by selecting edges in increasing order of weight.

⚙️ How it Works
Sort all edges by weight
Pick smallest edge
Check if it forms a cycle
If NO → add to MST
If YES → skip
Repeat until MST is complete

💡 Key Point
Uses Disjoint Set (Union-Find)

7️⃣ Dijkstra’s Algorithm (Shortest Path)
Finds shortest path from source to all vertices in weighted graph (no negative weights).

⚙️ How it Works
Initialize distances:
Source = 0
Others = ∞
Pick node with minimum distance
Update neighbors (relaxation)
Mark node as visited
Repeat

💡 Key Point
Always chooses nearest unvisited node
Greedy because it locks shortest path step-by-step
